abstract: "APIS (the Agent Passport Issuance Standard), published by Passport Alliance, is a cryptographic identity framework for autonomous AI agents: a credential chain of issuer, principal, delegate, mandate, machine/domain binding, and a signed agent passport, with algorithmic attestation tiers (TPM / confidential-compute / DNS-anchored), provider-neutral namespace proof, and model-scope mandates. v2.1 adds Tier 2.0 confidential-compute attestation, algorithmic tier resolution, provider-neutral DNS/HTTPS namespace proof, and a verified reference proof (Herman)."
